.TH VIEWSUN 1 "August 2026" "viewsun 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
viewsun \- fully custom tiling compositor (no X11/Wayland)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B viewsun
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B viewsun -w
\fI/path/to/wallpaper.png\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
viewsun is a from-scratch tiling window manager / compositor that talks directly to DRM/KMS and evdev.
It does not require X11 or Wayland. An SDL backend is included for testing inside a desktop session.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wallpaper " " \fIPATH\fR
Set wallpaper image (PNG, JPG, BMP). This is the required way to set the background:
.br
.B viewsun -w ~/wallpaper.jpg
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fIdrm|sdl|auto\fR
Select backend. \fBauto\fR tries DRM then falls back to SDL. Default: auto.
.TP
.BR \-\-card " " \fIPATH\fR
DRM card path, e.g. /dev/dri/card1. Default /dev/dri/card1.
.TP
.BR \-\-size " " \fIWIDTHxHEIGHT\fR
Force resolution (useful for SDL: \-\-size 1280x720).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version.
.SH CONTROLS
Super+Enter kitty
.br
Super+w browser
.br
Super+e file manager
.br
Super+P (Windows+P) logout
.br
Alt+Enter spawn placeholder
.br
Alt+q close focused
.br
Alt+Shift+q quit
.br
Alt+j/k focus
.br
Alt+h/l resize master
.br
Alt+m/b/g layouts (master/bsp/grid)
.br
Bottom bar shows time/date
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/viewsun/wallpaper.png
Default wallpaper if -w not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
viewsun -w /usr/share/backgrounds/wallpaper.jpg
.br
viewsun --backend sdl -w ./wall.jpg --size 1920x1080
.br
sudo viewsun --backend drm -w ~/wall.png
.SH AUTHOR
viewsun contributors.
